TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Final Report (Part 2): Space Mission Design","overview":"Develop a preliminary space-mission design that benefits Australia and report the mission concept and its space-segment elements. Use mission-design software of your choice, supported by hand calculations if useful, and justify the proposed design."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction: mission concept and rationale. Include the following required information: What is the spacecraft's primary mission? Why is the mission needed? How many spacecraft are used and why? Who are the users (operator and customers)?","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Addresses all requirements to a high standard. Detailed descriptions and discussions are included. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Addresses some requirements. Descriptions may feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Many or all requirements are not addressed. Poor descriptions or lack of appropriate referencing."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Main body: mission design. Present a summary of the mission design using software and/or hand calculations as appropriate. Include relevant screenshots and software files in the main body of the report and/or appendix. Include the following information: Where will it launch from, and using which launch vehicle? Why did you choose this option? What type of orbit will you use? What are its characteristics and orbital elements? Will you need to perform any orbital maneuvers? Which ground control facilities will you use? How often will your spacecraft be able to communicate with ground control? How long will the mission last, and what are your plans for EOL?","weight":60,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Demonstrates high level understanding of the design procedure. Design clearly addresses mission and course concepts. Major requirements are all addressed and are well supported with quality evidence (e.g. software screenshots, software files, hand calculations, references from literature). Content is comprehensive, accurate, and persuasive."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Demonstrates adequate understanding of the design procedure. Design may be inconsistent with regards to purpose and clarity of thought or feature errors. Major requirements are addressed but may lack some detail or are not well supported with evidence. Content may not be comprehensive and/or persuasive."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Demonstrates minimal understanding of the design procedure. Major requirements are not addressed and/or lack evidence. Content is incomplete or not persuasive."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Conclusion","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Detailed and appropriate conclusions reached from the evidence provided in the report."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Some conclusions are reached but they may be generic or lack specific detail."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful conclusions reached."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical engineering report structure. The report is easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Executive summary (or abstract) provides a concise overview of the report. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design > Launch"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design > Orbit"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Mission Design > Orbit; Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R7","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R8","met":"yes","where":"Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R9","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design > Orbit; Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R10","met":"partial","where":"Images 1-5; Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R11","met":"partial","where":"Whole report; Bibliography"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Design > Launch","issue":"Vega E is not yet operational; relying on a future launcher and unspecified rideshare creates schedule and interface risk."},{"where":"Mission Design > Orbit","issue":"Text says a very high altitude would yield low resolution images 'which is also desirable'; this is contradictory and should be undesirable."},{"where":"Mission Design > Orbit","issue":"RAAN initial value is said to indicate launch facility; RAAN at epoch depends on launch time/azimuth, not facility alone."},{"where":"Mission Design > Orbit","issue":"No swath/resolution calculation justifies 600 km for fluid lensing; 250 km reef width and daily coverage are not quantitatively linked."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"No link budget, data rate, ground antenna band, or contact capacity calculation; average contact duration alone is insufficient evidence for data transfer."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Claim that descending path is constantly sunlit and used for imaging is not demonstrated; SSO eclipse and LTAN are not specified."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"Drag-sail EOL is not sized or calculated; no demonstration of 25-year deorbit or re-entry casualty risk."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"Five-year life is assumed without propulsion/station-keeping or drag/SSO drift assessment."},{"where":"Images 1-5","issue":"Only screenshots are provided; no STK/PIGI files or model parameters are included."},{"where":"Bibliography","issue":"References are bare URLs, include Wikipedia, and [10] is malformed; no author/title/access dates."}],"overall":"Adequate report: mission concept and major design areas are covered with STK screenshots, but technical inconsistencies, missing software files, weak references and unnumbered figures/tables prevent an accomplished rating.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Introduction clearly explains coral-reef monitoring need, fluid-lensing mission, single-satellite rationale, and users/operator. References support rationale. Some claims are broad but all required elements are present to a high standard.","evidence":[{"where":"Introduction","quote":"The spacecraft is intended to image and send data to ground stations for collation and analysis."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Thus, only one satellite is required."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"The proposed satellite would likely be used by governmental and science agencies (e.g. CSIRO, BOM) for research and/or education."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":36.0,"max":60.0,"reasoning":"Covers launch, orbit, ground station, duration and EOL with STK screenshots and some calculations. However, launch relies on unbuilt Vega E, orbit/imaging rationale has contradictions, link and drag-sail sizing are absent, and STK files are not provided. Thus adequate, not accomplished.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Design > Orbit","quote":"an altitude of 600km requires a mean inclination of $ 97.7924^{\\circ} $ for the satellite to remain sun-synchronous."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"An average contact duration of almost ten minutes was achieved"},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"The most promising alternative is a ‘drag sail’"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":5.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Conclusion summarises launch, orbit and ground station, but omits duration, EOL, users and single-satellite rationale; it is largely generic and does not draw detailed quantitative conclusions.","evidence":[{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"A specific launch vehicle – the Vega E – has been selected although it has not been built yet."},{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"The Mt Pleasant Radio Observatory is well-located to receive data from this orbit type constantly and for long durations."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":10.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Structure and headings are clear, but figures/tables are not numbered consistently, references are bare URLs including Wikipedia, and grammar/typographical errors remain. Presentation is adequate but not professional.","evidence":[{"where":"Bibliography","quote":"[6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."},{"where":"Mission Design > Launch","quote":"a wiki sorted directory – ‘Timeline of spaceflight’ – will be referred to throughout the report [6]."},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""}]}]}
